{
  "_readme": "Documented allowlist for colour literals (hex/rgb()/hsl()) outside the token files. Every entry needs a category with a reason. `max` may only go DOWN (node scripts/color/check-colors.mjs --update-baseline lowers it). New files are never added automatically: convert to tokens, add `// color-ok: <reason>` on the line, or add an entry here in review.",
  "categories": {
    "brand-asset": "Brand marks, logo construction and the brand guide render the exact brand hex on purpose; they document or ARE the identity, so they must not follow theme tokens.",
    "tenant-brand-data": "Tenant-entered or tenant-default brand colours (hex strings stored in the database, colour pickers, validators, placeholders and \"must look like #1A2B3C\" hints). The value is data, not a Vireek theme colour.",
    "document-output": "PDF, print, e-mail HTML, QR codes, labels and exported canvases. These render outside the app DOM where CSS variables do not exist, so resolved hex is required.",
    "persisted-data-palette": "Categorical palettes stored with records or sent as data (zones, outcomes, graph node kinds, territories). Changing them needs a data migration; to be moved to viz tokens separately.",
    "token-docs": "Token documentation page: displays resolved hex values of the tokens on purpose.",
    "third-party-surface": "Embeddable badge/widget preview that must look identical on third-party sites regardless of the visitor's Vireek theme.",
    "forced-print-bw": "Print stylesheet forces pure black on white regardless of theme (ink/toner and legibility)."
  },
